{"timestamp":"2026-05-06T09:19:31.768Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Because there isn’t one authoritative `raw`.\n\n`loadObjectSigner` loads system and global git config, then merges the typed config with:\n\n```go\nmerged := config.Merge(sysCfg, globalCfg)\n```\n\nBut go-git’s `config.Merge` does not merge `Raw`. So the old-style direct check against `merged.Raw.Section(\"gpg\").Subsection(\"ssh\").Option(\"program\")` can miss the setting.\n\nThe loop in `customSignProgram` is doing two things:\n\n1. Checks each raw config source in precedence order: system, then global.\n2. Handles more than SSH: `gpg.program` for OpenPGP and `gpg.<format>.program` for SSH/OpenPGP/X509.\n\nFor just SSH, the core lookup could absolutely be the direct form inside the helper:\n\n```go\nraw.Section(\"gpg\").Subsection(\"ssh\").Option(\"program\")\n```\n\nThe only part I would not drop is iterating over `sysCfg.Raw` and `globalCfg.Raw`, because that is what preserves config precedence without relying on `merged.Raw`.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-06T09:19:31.768Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Because there isn’t one authoritative `raw`.\n\n`loadObjectSigner` loads system and global git config, then merges the typed config with:\n\n```go\nmerged := config.Merge(sysCfg, globalCfg)\n```\n\nBut go-git’s `config.Merge` does not merge `Raw`. So the old-style direct check against `merged.Raw.Section(\"gpg\").Subsection(\"ssh\").Option(\"program\")` can miss the setting.\n\nThe loop in `customSignProgram` is doing two things:\n\n1. Checks each raw config source in precedence order: system, then global.\n2. Handles more than SSH: `gpg.program` for OpenPGP and `gpg.<format>.program` for SSH/OpenPGP/X509.\n\nFor just SSH, the core lookup could absolutely be the direct form inside the helper:\n\n```go\nraw.Section(\"gpg\").Subsection(\"ssh\").Option(\"program\")\n```\n\nThe only part I would not drop is iterating over `sysCfg.Raw` and `globalCfg.Raw`, because that is what preserves config precedence without relying on `merged.Raw`."}],"phase":"final_answer"}}
